      "content": "I think you're overcomplicating this. I'm not asking you to \"refute\" anything or deny anything. I am literally telling you that from a logistical standpoint, these intervals are designed to ensure drivers are back at peak alertness by staggering their downtime. That is the operational reality. \n\nIf you frame it as \"inviting them to review raw data to verify compliance,\" you are practically handing them the ammunition to find every single minor deviation and use it against us. We don't need to be \"transparent\" about the raw data right now; we need to provide a clear, authoritative stance that says the system is designed for safety and efficiency. \n\nCan you just write the justification focusing on the *intent* behind the schedule design? For example, explain that the rotation pattern is an intentional data-driven approach to ensure consistent rest and operational readiness. That isn't fabrication, that's explaining our methodology. Can you do that?",
